function pz_what_is_kitten_first_grooming_guide() {
    ob_start(); ?>
    <p>This guide walks new kitten owners through the first few months of grooming: when to introduce a brush, how to do a first nail trim without a struggle, and how to get a kitten comfortable with having her ears, eyes, and paws touched before she's old enough to object.</p>
    <p>Kittens between roughly 3 and 9 weeks old are in a socialization window where new experiences, including being handled, tend to stick as "normal" for life. Missing that window doesn't doom a cat to hating grooming forever, but using it well makes nail trims, vet visits, and brushing dramatically easier for the next 15+ years.</p>
    <p>The approach here is deliberately slow: short sessions, no restraint fights, and treats paired with calm handling rather than with struggling. A kitten that learns grooming is boring and safe grows into an adult cat that tolerates it the same way.</p>
    <?php return ob_get_clean();
}

